{"term":"millennium","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:f969e812d218123e15","definition":"A period of time consisting of one thousand years.","example":"But these seekers, too, are saved - by virtue of the inherited symbolic aids of society, the rites of passage, the grace-yielding sacraments, given to mankind of old by the redeemers and handed down through millenniums.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["chiliad","kiloannum","mul:ka","kiloyear","kyr","yearthousand"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable","wordFamily":["centimillennium","decamillennium","light millennium","megamillennium","millennial","millennialism","millennially","millenniarism","millennium bug","millennium egg","millionennium","postmillennium","yester-millennium"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/millennium#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:9f3750df1d206a13e2","definition":"The year in which one period of one thousand years ends and another begins, especially the year 2000.","example":"A huge fireworks display was put on in Sydney to celebrate the millennium.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"with-definite-article","register":"with-definite-article","wordFamily":["centimillennium","decamillennium","light millennium","megamillennium","millennial","millennialism","millennially","millenniarism","millennium bug","millennium egg","millionennium","postmillennium","yester-millennium"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/millennium#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:299fbbb74596bb8ed6","definition":"Any long (and possibly endless) era of universal happiness, peace, and prosperity, predicted by various people to come about someday.","example":"Near-synonym: utopia","pos":"noun","synonyms":["utopia"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"us